Z||000000||FieroRyan||10-22-2001||10:28 PM||||Some stupid lady in her Miata bumped me while I was taking a left today.  It was rainy out, so the bump threw me all the way around and (eventually) ended up about 15 feet into a ravine/deep ditch.  4 hours later, $140 towing fee + $700-800 body damage est.  I only have liability...<P>Does anyone have a spare notchback clip or a fastback conversion for around $400?  That's all I can get (if that) within the next few days...  and my car is really screwed up bodywise.  Amazingly it still runs fine though...  mechanically sound.<P><BR>Thus ends my days horror story  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||Brandon86SE||10-22-2001||10:43 PM||||umm.... who cares if you only have liability, that has nothing to do with this case.  You're not at fault.  Whenever someone is rear-ended it is the rear-enders fault.  That means she (her insurance company) pays for all your damages!  I just don't wanna see a fellow Fiero owner get screwed here....  Best of luck....<P>Brandon||||reg||1
Z||000002||northstarfieroorbust||10-22-2001||11:06 PM||||Ive got an 85 se that i wrapped around a telephone pole, head on, so the rear end is in great shape, i plan on stripping the car down to sell the parts. Ive never pulled the rear facia or notch section off one befor, but i could try if the price is right||||reg||1
Z||000003||Pontiaddict||10-22-2001||11:07 PM||||In most states, if you have liability all you're going to get is a few hundred dollars. The insurance compainies lobbied  for laws like that becasue they claim that if you don't have full coverage on your car that it isn't worth paying for.||||reg||1
Z||000004||sqoach||10-22-2001||11:56 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Pontiaddict:<BR><B>In most states, if you have liability all you're going to get is a few hundred dollars. The insurance compainies lobbied  for laws like that becasue they claim that if you don't have full coverage on your car that it isn't worth paying for.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That's total bullshit!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif"><P>Not you, just the law. I haven't heard of that. Not worth paying for!?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">  You're paying them your money to have your car insured! If something like that happens, I would be extremely pissed!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> What the hell are you paying them for if they're not gonna pay you the damages!?!?<BR>I was in a wreck two years ago, not my fault, and all I had was liability. They paid for the repairs, and my medical bill. Had to go to the chiropractor(sp?) for back/neck injuries. It was a total of $2600. $700+ for the medical bill, the rest for the car. I forgot exactly what happened, but I think they ruled the car (bronco) totaled. Then my dad bought it back, and we fixed it ourselves, getting parts from a local junkyard. Probably cost us $100 to fix. I got the rest of the money   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>               <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">               <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">               <BR>^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><LI>86 SC 2.5L 5spd</FONT><p>[This message has been edited by sqoach (edited 10-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||lowCG||10-23-2001||12:44 AM||||Sounds like what happened to me awhile back,but anyways,it's the responsibility of the driver at fault(her)to fix your car.<BR>In some states they have a "no fault" policy where everyone fixes their own car;not so in WA state.<BR>Good luck finding a decent place to fix it,the only shop I found around here that would touch it was behind the Toyota dealer in Burien(not the Toyota bodyshop)and they suck.||||reg||1
Z||000006||beer_stud_21||10-23-2001||12:54 AM||||We have "No Fault" here in hawaii.  Everyone doesn't pay for their own car though.  "No Fault" means you are insuring yourself for damages you cause, both to the other car and people (up to a certain $$ amount of course).  Anything above that you are liable for out of your own pocket.  Full coverage gets you coverage for damages you cause, or damages caused by uninsured motorists.  Statistically something like 1/3 of people on the roads here are uninsured, even though its illegal to drive without it!  Insurance is really expensive here (as well as everything else!)<P>-Marlin||||reg||1
Z||000007||FieroRyan||10-23-2001||12:55 AM||||...And if she sped off?<P>I don't know her, I didn't get her plates (at the time i was spinning into a ditch)...<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||stimpy||10-23-2001||01:13 AM||||I sure do hope you called the cops and reported it as a hit and run. Do you live in a smaller town? Newspapers in little burg eat that kind of story up. Contact them and get Crimestoppers to offer a reward. If this cold beeyatch can spin you into a ditch filled with water and drive off, she's probably pissed domeone else off enough to drop a dime on her. Next time she'll probably be running down a kid on a big wheel or a (God forbid) a box of kittens...||||reg||1
